1. DEFINITIONS

"The Software" means the Pavise program, together with the source code, binaries,
icons and documentation distributed with this licence.

"Derivative Version" means any work that modifies, translates or adapts the
Software, or that incorporates all or part of its code.

"The Author" means bdth (2074055628@qq.com).


2. GRANT OF RIGHTS

Subject to full compliance with this licence, anyone may, free of charge:

1. Use the Software for any purpose, including personal use and internal use
   within organisations such as companies, internet cafes and esports venues;
2. Copy the Software and distribute it to others free of charge;
3. Modify the Software, create Derivative Versions, and distribute those
   Derivative Versions to others free of charge;
4. Read, study and reference the Software's source code.


3. NO SALE

Charging any fee in connection with the distribution of the Software or a
Derivative Version is prohibited in any form. This includes, without limitation:

1. Selling copies, activation keys, accounts or download access for the Software
   or a Derivative Version;
2. Supplying the Software or a Derivative Version as part of, as a bonus to, or
   as added value for any paid product, paid service or subscription service;
3. Placing the Software behind a paywall, paid download, paid unlock, donation
   gate, or any other arrangement in which payment is a condition of obtaining it;
4. Preinstalling the Software or a Derivative Version on devices, system images
   or complete machines that are sold for money;
5. Distributing the Software or a Derivative Version in exchange for non-monetary
   consideration, such as revenue sharing, or using it to drive traffic towards
   other paid offerings.

Voluntary donations are not prohibited by this section, provided that payment is
never a condition of obtaining the Software, any of its features, or any form of
technical support.

Commercial use of the Software in any of the ways described above requires prior
written authorisation from the Author. Contact 2074055628@qq.com.


4. OBLIGATIONS WHEN DISTRIBUTING

When distributing the Software or a Derivative Version, you must:

1. Retain this licence text, the copyright notice and the author information in
   full;
2. Clearly inform recipients that the Software may not be sold, and that they are
   equally bound by this licence;
3. When distributing a Derivative Version, clearly state who modified it and what
   was changed.


5. NAME AND MARKS

The "Pavise" name, icon and interface marks are not covered by the rights granted
under this licence.

A Derivative Version must be released under a name and icon clearly distinct from
those of the Software. It may not be released as Pavise, nor in any other manner
likely to suggest that it originates from the Author.


6. TERMINATION

Any breach of this licence terminates all rights granted under it immediately and
automatically. Rights are not automatically restored by subsequently curing the
breach. Continued use or distribution after termination constitutes infringement.

The Author may, at their sole discretion, reinstate the rights upon receiving a
written explanation.


7. DISCLAIMER

The Software is provided "AS IS", without warranty of any kind, express or
implied, including but not limited to the warranties of merchantability, fitness
for a particular purpose and non-infringement.

The Software modifies process scheduling parameters, system power and display
settings, registry values and service states, and may apply resource suppression
to anti-cheat programs. Users must assess the associated risks themselves.

In no event shall the Author be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental,
special or consequential damages arising from the use of or inability to use the
